msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:82
msgid ""
"AutoSchedule creates exactly one TaskNode for the complete marker body. "
"Statements issue in source order without internal synchronization, so each "
"preceding statement contributes its II and only the final statement exposes "
"its latency. All statements must use one Ascend hardware pipe and one AIC/"
"AIV core affinity; split cross-pipe or cross-core sequences into separate "
"tasks. The marker does not select or launch a core by itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:89
msgid ""
"``latency`` is the number of cycles from task issue until its outputs are "
"ready. ``ii`` is the minimum interval before the same hardware pipe may "
"issue another instance. Task costs require ``latency >= ii``. Either value "
"may be omitted, in which case the ``EstimateLatency`` pass supplies it and "
"validates the final pair. Provided values are trusted exact overrides for "
"the complete task body, not hints for the enclosing loop II. These are the "
"only public task parameters. The compiler derives execution resources from "
"the task body and determines core placement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:98
msgid ""
"Inside ``T.PerCoreTask()``, the same marker also denotes one concrete per-"
"core candidate. Put the control flow that selects a core outside this scope "
"so automatic synchronization remains under the same guard. Explicit markers "
"may be mixed with unmarked candidates; the compiler infers markers for the "
"remaining supported candidate boundaries. Do not nest ``T.PerCoreTask()`` "
"inside this scope; put this ``T.Task()`` inside ``T.PerCoreTask()`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:122
msgid ""
"If any direct child task or loop in a scheduled child list has a ``T.Stage`` "
"annotation, AutoSchedule treats that child list as manual. One scope may "
"contain several consecutive statements; every scheduler task materialized "
"from those statements receives the same stage. Unannotated siblings default "
"to stage 0. Within each hardware pipe, source order is the manual issue "
"order; tasks on different pipes remain freely reorderable, so no separate "
"order annotation is required. Nested child lists select automatic or manual "
"scheduling independently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:131
msgid ""
"``T.Stage`` must wrap complete scheduler tasks. It must not appear inside "
"``T.Task``, ``T.SimtVF``, ``T.SimdVF``, an SBlock, or a parallel loop. In "
"Python's multi-context form, put ``T.Stage`` first so it is the outer scope:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:135
msgid ""
"# Correct\n"
"with T.Stage(1), T.SimtVF(threads=128):\n"
"    ...\n"
"\n"
"# Invalid: T.Stage is nested inside the SimtVF task boundary\n"
"with T.SimtVF(threads=128), T.Stage(1):\n"
"    ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:145
msgid ""
"Non-zero stages require an enclosing loop with ``enable_offset=True``. ``T."
"Pipelined(..., num_stages=...)`` controls the automatic buffer-version "
"search bound; it does not limit the values accepted by ``T.Stage``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:160
msgid ""
"Assert that two buffer regions do not conflict, suppressing a false "
"dependency the auto-scheduler would otherwise conservatively insert."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:163
msgid ""
"The auto-scheduler's dependency analysis cannot prove that dynamically "
"indexed accesses (e.g. a permutation ``state_cache[perm[idx], ...]``) are "
"disjoint across loop iterations, so it inserts redundant synchronization. "
"This hint lets the user declare that the regions do not overlap. It is "
"consumed by the ``NormalizeConflictHints`` pass before auto-scheduling; at "
"runtime it is a no-op."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:170
msgid ""
"first region -- ``buffer[indices...]`` or a bare ``buffer`` (the whole "
"buffer). A region must exactly match the footprint of the access it refers "
"to: use slices for the accessed extents (e.g. ``buf[i, 0:M, 0:N]``), since a "
"fully scalar-indexed ``buf[i, 0, 0]`` denotes only a 1-element region and "
"will not match a wider copy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:175
msgid "second region; defaults to ``a`` (a self-dependency)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:176
msgid ""
"where the non-overlap is asserted. ``None`` applies it to the outermost "
"sequence represented by ``tilelang_root`` and independently to every loop "
"enclosing both operands. ``-1`` applies it only to the outermost sequence. "
"Non-negative values select one common enclosing loop, counted from the "
"outermost (``0`` = outermost, ``1`` = next inner, ...)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:182
msgid ""
"``None`` = both same- and cross-iteration are conflict-free (default); "
"``True`` = only cross-iteration; ``False`` = only same-iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:185
msgid ""
"string tag pairing two separately-written half-declarations whose regions "
"live in different scopes (so they cannot be written in one call). Must "
"appear exactly twice; the combined hint is attached to the loops enclosing "
"both. Rarely needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:211
msgid ""
"This is the conservative counterpart of :func:`assume_no_conflict`.  It "
"makes the auto-scheduler treat matching accesses as if they used the same "
"storage, even when the buffers are distinct or their regions are provably "
"disjoint.  The usual RAW, WAR, and WAW rules still apply: two read-only "
"accesses do not form a dependency.  The marker is consumed before auto-"
"scheduling and is a runtime no-op."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:218
msgid ""
"first region -- ``buffer[indices...]`` or a bare ``buffer`` (the whole "
"buffer). A concrete region must exactly match the footprint of the access it "
"refers to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:221
msgid "second region; defaults to ``a`` (a forced self-conflict)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:222
msgid ""
"where the conflict is asserted. ``None`` applies it to the outermost "
"sequence represented by ``tilelang_root`` and independently to every loop "
"enclosing both operands. ``-1`` applies it only to the outermost sequence. "
"Non-negative values select one common enclosing loop, counted from the "
"outermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:227
msgid ""
"``None`` = both same- and cross-iteration conflicts (default); ``True`` = "
"only cross-iteration; ``False`` = only same-iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/schedule_hint/index.rst:229
msgid ""
"string tag pairing two declarations in different scopes. It must appear "
"exactly twice. With ``level=None``, declarations with no common serial loop "
"are still related at the root sequence."
msgstr ""
